.TH DARQOS-UPDATE 8 2026-11-13 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
darqos\-update \- install an update requested from within DarqOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /darq/bin/darqos\-update
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B darqos\-update
installs an update that the
.I Update DarqOS
tool, on the Terminal's Tools panel, has requested.
DarqOS runs as
.BR darq ,
which can't install anything, so the tool leaves a distribution
tarball,
.IR darqos.tar.gz ,
its signature,
.IR darqos.tar.gz.sig ,
and a request,
.IR request ,
in
.IR /darq/run/update .
.I darqos\-update.path
sees the request, and starts
.IR darqos\-update.service ,
which runs
.B darqos\-update
as root.
The request is
.B action=update
or
.BR action=reinstall .
.PP
It performs these steps, stopping, with a result that says why, if any
fails:
.IP 1. 4
Copy the tarball and its signature into
.IR /var/lib/darqos/update ,
out of
.BR darq 's
reach, so what's checked is what's installed, and remove the request.
.IP 2.
Check the signature, with
.BR "ssh\-keygen \-Y verify" ,
in the
.B darqos\-release
namespace, against the installed release key,
.IR /etc/darqos/allowed_signers .
An update never changes the key: a new key is installed by hand, with
.BR dui (8).
.IP 3.
Refuse a tarball whose version is older than what's installed, by
edition and then build, or the same, unless it's a reinstall: going
back is done by hand, with
.BR dui (8).
.IP 4.
Back up, with
.IR darqos\-backup.service ,
and stop if the backup fails.
.IP 5.
Run the tarball's own
.BR dui (8),
with
.BR \-\-update ,
which stops DarqOS, installs it, and starts DarqOS again.
.IP 6.
Leave a result,
.IR /darq/run/update/result ,
for the Terminal, which shows it once, after unlocking:
.B outcome=ok
or
.BR outcome=failed ,
with what was installed, what is now, why, and the log.
.PP
With no request, it does nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
For tests:
.BR DARQ ,
the installation root;
.BR LOG_DIR ;
.BR CONF_DIR ,
where the release key is;
.BR DARQOS_UPDATE_STAGING ,
in place of
.IR /var/lib/darqos/update ;
.BR DARQOS_BACKUP ,
a command in place of the backup; and
.BR DARQOS_DUI ,
a command in place of the tarball's
.BR dui .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /darq/run/update
The request, the tarball and its signature, and the result.
.TP
.I /var/lib/darqos/update
Where the tarball's checked, and installed from.
.TP
.I /etc/darqos/allowed_signers
The installed release key.
.TP
.I /var/log/darqos/update-*.log
What it did.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if it installed, or there was nothing to do; 1 if it refused, or
failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dui (8),
.BR install (8),
.BR darqos\-backup (8),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1)
